**Backend changes**

Read the flag in the PUT handler. Multipart sends strings and JSON sends booleans, so accept both. Ignore the flag when a file is present:

```js
const removeRequested = req.body?.removePhoto === true || req.body?.removePhoto === 'true';
const removePhoto = !req.file && removeRequested; // new file wins
```

Pass it as parameter `$5` and update the SQL. Use `$1::text` so Postgres can infer the type in the `CASE` expression:

```sql
UPDATE plants
   SET name = COALESCE($2, name),
       interval_days = COALESCE($3, interval_days),
       photo_url = CASE
         WHEN $1::text IS NOT NULL THEN $1::text
         WHEN $5::boolean THEN NULL
         ELSE photo_url
       END
 WHERE id = $4
 RETURNING id, name, interval_days, photo_url
```

Update the query params to `[photoUrl, name?.trim() ?? null, interval, id, removePhoto]`.

