- **Tests:** the mock in `photo.test.js` reads `params[0] ?? EXISTING_PHOTO`, so it needs to return `null` when `params[4]` is true. Add a test that sends `{ removePhoto: true }` and expects `photoUrl` to be `null`.
- **Disk cleanup (optional):** removing the photo leaves the old file in `/uploads`. Fetch the old `photo_url` in the same request and unlink it after the update succeeds, or run a periodic sweep for unreferenced files.

This adds a `SELECT` before the `UPDATE` so the handler knows the previous `photo_url`. After the update succeeds, it deletes the old file if the photo was cleared. I also delete the old file when a new one replaces it, since otherwise it becomes an orphan. Remove that branch if you want strict "cleared only" behavior.

