A single `onPlantSaved` prop can't do both jobs. A function that the list calls can't also be the way the list receives a saved plant. `PlantsList` also never saves anything, so it has no point where it would naturally call `onPlantSaved`. I've split the two directions into separate props:

- `savedPlant` (in): the parent passes the latest saved plant. The list upserts it into local state.
- `onChange` (out): the list tells the parent the new full array after delete, clear, or upsert, so the parent can stay in sync.

