```

Notes:
- `commit` is the only place that changes the list after load, so `onPlantsChange` always receives the same array the component is rendering.
- `onPlantSaved` is called only for upserts. `onPlantsChange` is called for upserts, deletes, and clears, and it fires after `onPlantSaved` on an upsert.
- A parent that passes `savedPlant` should also pass `onPlantsChange` if it needs the full list. Otherwise it only sees the single plant.

Top-level `plants` state isn't needed here. `PlantsList` keeps its own list and reads from storage on mount, so `App` only has to hold `lastSaved`. I've left out `onPlantsChange`, since nothing above `PlantsList` uses the full array.

`onPlantSaved` also isn't strictly necessary, because `PlantForm` already sets `lastSaved`. Calling `setLastSaved` again with the same object is a no-op for React, so it's harmless, and it keeps `App` in sync if the list ever upserts a plant from another source.

